---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactBand from '../../components/layout/ContactBand.astro';
import ProjectMetadata from '../../components/project/ProjectMetadata.astro';
import { projects } from '../../data/projects';
import '../../styles/askwill.css';

const project = projects.find((item) => item.slug === 'askwill');
if (!project) throw new Error('AskWill project record is missing.');
---

<BaseLayout
  approvedMobileContact
  title="Rebuilding AskWill.ca"
  description="A full website rethink for a family-run water-service business, covering structure, content, SEO, privacy, and QA."
  canonicalPath={project.route}
>
<article class="askwill-case"><header class="askwill-hero">
<h1>Rebuilding AskWill.ca</h1>
<p class="askwill-lede">I built the original AskWill site in Wix and maintained it for several years. It worked well, although visually it had a bit of an “amateur PowerPoint deck” vibe. Over that time, I conducted usability testing and monitored customer feedback and GA4 data to identify opportunities for improvement. By the time I rebuilt it, I had a pretty good idea of what I wanted to change.</p>
<p class="askwill-lede">For the rebuild, I organized the service pages around recognizable problems such as staining and odour, and made the owner’s contact options more prominent. I also migrated the site from Wix to an Astro-based build hosted on Cloudflare.</p>
<ProjectMetadata tags={project.tags} />
<dl aria-label="Project context" class="askwill-facts">
<div><dt>Business</dt><dd>Family-run water-treatment and well-services business</dd></div>
<div><dt>Result</dt><dd>19-page site now live at <a class="askwill-live-link" href="https://askwill.ca/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">AskWill.ca</a></dd></div>
</dl>
</header><div class="askwill-reasoning-bridge askwill-reasoning-bridge--single">
<section aria-labelledby="maintenance-title" class="askwill-section askwill-section--lessons">
<div class="askwill-intro askwill-intro--lessons-centered">
<div><p class="askwill-eyebrow">Version 1</p><h2 id="maintenance-title">What maintaining the first site taught me</h2></div>
</div>
<div class="askwill-decisions" role="list">
<div role="listitem"><p><span>V1</span>Small layout changes could take too much work and affect nearby elements.</p><p><span>V2</span>Reusable components and explicit CSS rules.</p></div>
<div role="listitem"><p><span>V1</span>Desktop and mobile layouts could behave differently than expected.</p><p><span>V2</span>Defined responsive rules and repeatable viewport testing.</p></div>
<div role="listitem"><p><span>V1</span>Changes were difficult to review before publishing.</p><p><span>V2</span>A source-controlled workflow where changes could be tested and reviewed before going live.</p></div>
</div>
</section>
</div><section class="askwill-section askwill-section--research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
<div class="askwill-intro">
<div><p class="askwill-eyebrow">Research behind the rebuild</p><h2 id="research-title">Listening before rearranging</h2></div>
<p>I analyzed 1000+ customer inquiries and search queries and moderated 15+ interviews/usability sessions to understand customers’ questions, terminology and points of confusion. Those findings helped me decide what to make clearer, what to bring forward, and where people needed an easier way to reach Will.</p>
</div>
</section><section aria-labelledby="visual-direction-title" class="askwill-section askwill-section--visual">
<div class="askwill-intro">
<div><p class="askwill-eyebrow">Visual direction</p><h2 id="visual-direction-title">A cleaner visual system</h2></div>
<p>Version 1 had the right identity, but over time the presentation had become visually busy. For the rebuild, I kept the familiar AskWill colours and Will's owner-led presence while simplifying the hierarchy, spacing, typography, and overall page structure.</p>
</div>
<figure aria-label="AskWill homepage hero before and after" class="askwill-comparison askwill-home-comparison">
<div class="askwill-compare-grid">
<div class="askwill-panel"><p class="askwill-panel-label">V1 · Wix</p><div class="askwill-browser"><div aria-hidden="true" class="askwill-browser-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="askwill-media-window askwill-media-window--home"><img alt="Authentic crop of the original AskWill Wix homepage hero." src="/assets/projects/askwill/case-home-wix-approved.png" width="1004" height="548"/></div></div></div>
<div class="askwill-panel"><p class="askwill-panel-label">V2 · Rebuild</p><div class="askwill-browser"><div aria-hidden="true" class="askwill-browser-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="askwill-media-window askwill-media-window--home"><img alt="Parker-supplied current AskWill homepage screenshot showing the rebuilt desktop homepage." src="/assets/projects/askwill/case-home-rebuilt-approved.png" width="1088" height="617"/></div></div></div>
</div>
</figure>
</section><section aria-labelledby="clearest-change" class="askwill-section askwill-section--comparison">
<div class="askwill-intro">
<div><p class="askwill-eyebrow">Services</p><h2 id="clearest-change"><span class="askwill-services-title-line">Starting with</span> <span class="askwill-services-title-line">the problem</span></h2></div>
<div class="askwill-intro-copy">
<p>Version 1 already had detailed service pages, but customers often knew the problem they were seeing before they knew which service or equipment they needed.</p>
<p>The rebuilt Services page lets homeowners start with problems such as hard water, staining, odour, or low pressure, then points them toward the relevant service.</p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="services-comparison-title" aria-label="AskWill Services page before and after" class="askwill-comparison" data-kind="services">
<div class="askwill-compare-grid">
<div class="askwill-panel">
<p class="askwill-panel-label">V1 · Wix</p>
<div class="askwill-browser"><div aria-hidden="true" class="askwill-browser-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="askwill-media-window"><img alt="Parker-supplied Wix Services screenshot showing the original service-directory card grid." src="/assets/projects/askwill/case-services-wix-approved.png" width="1004" height="548"/></div></div>
</div>
<div class="askwill-panel">
<p class="askwill-panel-label">V2 · Rebuild</p>
<div class="askwill-browser"><div aria-hidden="true" class="askwill-browser-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><div class="askwill-media-window"><img alt="Parker-supplied current AskWill Services screenshot showing the symptom-led service guide." src="/assets/projects/askwill/case-services-rebuilt-approved.png" width="1088" height="621"/></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section><section aria-labelledby="system-title" class="askwill-section askwill-section--system">
<div class="askwill-intro">
<div><p class="askwill-eyebrow">The rebuild</p><h2 id="system-title"><span class="askwill-system-title-line">Structure, SEO,</span> <span class="askwill-system-title-line">and hosting</span></h2></div>
<p>I defined the site structure, content, SEO requirements, hosting and deployment needs, and QA criteria, then reviewed the implementation against those requirements.</p>
</div>
<div class="askwill-b-grid" aria-label="Rebuild structure, SEO, and hosting decisions">
<div class="askwill-b-left">
<section class="askwill-b-block"><p class="askwill-mini">Site structure</p><ul><li>Clearer distinctions between related services</li><li>Reusable page patterns across the site</li><li>Direct contact with Will kept prominent</li></ul></section>
<section class="askwill-b-block"><p class="askwill-mini">SEO migration</p><ul><li>Explicit control over routes, redirects, canonicals, and indexation</li><li>Preserved established service URLs <span class="askwill-no-break">during rebuild</span></li><li>Kept organic service pages and paid-search landing pages separate</li></ul></section>
</div>
<section class="askwill-b-host" aria-label="Hosting and deployment">
<p class="askwill-mini">Hosting &amp; deployment</p>
<ul><li>Static Astro site served through Cloudflare</li><li>Small serverless layer for lead-form requests</li><li>Source-controlled updates instead of publishing directly from Wix</li></ul>
<hr>
<p class="askwill-host-detail">To reduce ongoing platform costs (Wix was costing more than $400 a year) and keep the site lightweight, I decided not to move AskWill to another visual site builder. The rebuild uses a static Astro site served through Cloudflare, with a small serverless layer handling lead forms and Resend delivering the emails. Moving away from the visual-builder model also gave me more predictable control over responsive behaviour and SEO details such as routes, redirects, canonicals, and indexation. Future updates are easier to test, review, and publish without relying on the Wix editor.</p>
</section>
</div>

</section><section aria-labelledby="validation-title" class="askwill-section askwill-section--qa">
<div class="askwill-intro">
<div><p class="askwill-eyebrow">QA</p><h2 id="validation-title">Testing the rebuild</h2></div>
<p>Before launch, I tested the rebuild at both the source and browser level, covering responsive layouts, forms, keyboard and accessibility behaviour, privacy and security checks, and multiple browser engines.</p>
</div>
<div aria-label="AskWill rebuild validation evidence" class="askwill-proof askwill-proof--approved">
<div><strong>199</strong><span>source tests</span></div>
<div><strong>399</strong><span>QA groups</span></div>
<div><strong>72</strong><span>screenshots and browser captures reviewed</span></div>
<div><strong>Firefox + WebKit</strong><span>cross-engine checks</span></div>
</div>
</section><section aria-label="Final live result" class="askwill-section askwill-section--live-final"><p class="askwill-live-result">The rebuilt site is now live at <a class="askwill-live-link" href="https://askwill.ca/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">AskWill.ca</a>.</p></section></article>
  <ContactBand mobileEmailLabel />
</BaseLayout>
